{
  "case_id": "2020-20-297",
  "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A class of 8,185 individuals with OFAC alerts in their credit fles sued TransUnion under the Fair Credit Reporting Act for failing to use reasonable procedures to ensure the accuracy of their credit fles."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "TransUnion",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But TransUnion advances a per- suasive argument that the mere risk of future harm, without more, cannot qualify as a concrete harm in a suit for damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States as amicus curiae asserts that the plaintiffs suffered a concrete \u201cinformational injury\u201d from TransUnion's formatting violations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "total award of more than $60 million. The District Court rejected all of TransUnion's post-trial motions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted certiorari. 592 U. S. \u2013\u2013\u2013 (2020)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question in this case is whether the 8,185 class members have Article III standing as to their three claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In sum, under Article III, a federal court may resolve only \u201ca real controversy with real impact on real persons.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0001-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But under Article III, an injury in law is not an injury in fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0001-0007",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Every class member must have Article III standing in order to recover individual damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The plaintiffs argue that the publication to a third party of a credit report bearing a misleading OFAC alert injures the subject of the report."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have no trouble concluding that the 1,853 class members suffered a concrete harm that qualifes as an injury in fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "TransUnion",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "TransUnion counters that those 1,853 class members did not suffer a harm with a \u201cclose relationship\u201d to defamation because the OFAC alerts on the disseminated credit reports were only misleading and not literally false."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "TransUnion",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "TransUnion advances a persuasive argument that in a suit for damages, the mere risk of future harm, standing alone, cannot qualify as a concrete harm\u2014at least unless the exposure to the risk of future harm itself causes a separate concrete harm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "TransUnion generated credit reports that erroneously fagged many law-abiding people as potential terrorists and drug traffckers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0004-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "inherently insuffcient to support standing. 5 And never before has this Court declared that legislatures are constitutionally precluded from creating legal rights enforceable in federal court if those rights deviate too far from their common-law roots. According to the majority, courts alone have the power to sift and weigh harms to decide whether they merit the Federal Judiciary's attention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0004-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that the plaintiffs actually did not allege that they failed to receive any required information; they alleged only that they received it in the \u201cwrong format.\u201d Ante, at 441."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0004-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "did not receive the OFAC credit reports they had requested. Tr. of Oral Arg. 9."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0004-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "* * * Ultimately, the majority seems to pose to the reader a single rhetorical question: Who could possibly think that a person is harmed when he requests and is sent an incomplete credit report, or is sent a suspicious notice informing him that he may be a designated drug traffcker or terrorist, or is not sent anything informing him of how to remove this inaccurate red fag? The answer is, of course, legion: Congress, the President, the jury, the District Court, the Ninth Circuit, and four Members of this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-20-297",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "999fb878304c48611e3eebbbabd9f9eca746849fd296c5a12a59e1f9609824b6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-999fb878304c-0004-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "456 (Thomas, J., dissenting) (noting that \u201cnearly 25 percent of the class\u201d already had false reports \u201csent to potential creditors\u201d). And in addressing the claims of faulty disclosure to the plaintiffs, the majority makes a set of curious assumptions."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
